WEBVTT
NOTE SYNC_TYPE: HUMAN_VERIFIED
NOTE Track: 1-08 - Artificial Gravity
NOTE Artist: The Stardust Engine
NOTE Album: Mile Marker 98 (2003)

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:41.027
[Instrumental Intro — Raw Acoustic Guitar & Heartbeat Kick Drum]

00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:46.800
The natural physics don't apply to me no more

00:00:47.628 --> 00:00:51.869
I can't feel the boots resting on the cabin floor

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:59.811
The medical bay is quiet and the damage is done

00:01:01.251 --> 00:01:05.452
I'm a stationary moon staring at a distant sun

00:01:08.107 --> 00:01:12.450
I've got the six strings resting heavy on my knee

00:01:14.612 --> 00:01:20.500
Trying to remember how the Engine used to be

00:01:21.577 --> 00:01:26.800
My hands are still calloused, my grip is still tight

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.885
Just trying to find the gravity in the middle of the night

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:39.032
The thrusters are cold, the lower decks are dark

00:01:39.072 --> 00:01:42.500
But I'm blowing on the embers of a heavy metal spark

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.800
If the planet won't hold me, if the orbit is dead

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:50.000
I'm gonna have to spin the metal hull instead!

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.500
Artificial Gravity!

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.500
Building up the pressure inside of me!

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.200
Artificial Gravity!

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.424
A heavy rotation so the pilot can see!

00:02:03.484 --> 00:02:07.565
If the natural pull is permanently gone

00:02:07.585 --> 00:02:13.500
I'll engineer the weight just to carry on!

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.187
Making my own Artificial Gravity!

00:02:23.703 --> 00:02:28.566
It's a stalemate year in the center of the void

00:02:30.047 --> 00:02:35.800
Picking up the pieces of the ship that got destroyed

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:42.500
I'm mapping out the protocols, tracking every hour

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:48.379
Rerouting the cables to the auxiliary power

00:02:50.978 --> 00:02:57.200
I can't stand up to look out of the glass

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:02.287
But I can feel the friction of the cosmic dust pass

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.082
The thrusters are cold, the lower decks are dark

00:03:08.142 --> 00:03:11.500
But I'm blowing on the embers of a heavy metal spark

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.800
If the planet won't hold me, if the orbit is dead

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.000
I'm gonna have to spin the metal hull instead!

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.500
Artificial Gravity!

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.500
Building up the pressure inside of me!

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.200
Artificial Gravity!

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.436
A heavy rotation so the pilot can see!

00:03:32.496 --> 00:03:36.558
If the natural pull is permanently gone

00:03:36.598 --> 00:03:42.500
I'll engineer the weight just to carry on!

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.941
Making my own Artificial Gravity!

00:03:45.941 --> 00:04:20.095
[Guitar Solo]

00:04:20.095 --> 00:04:26.800
The engine is quiet, but it hasn't stopped.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:33.700
The pressure is holding, the anchor is dropped.

00:04:33.804 --> 00:04:37.287
I'm spinning the wheel, I'm finding the ground.

00:04:37.327 --> 00:04:40.369
I'm pulling the weight from the inside out!

00:04:42.727 --> 00:04:46.200
Artificial Gravity!

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.200
Building up the pressure inside of me!

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.000
Artificial Gravity!

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.554
A heavy rotation so the pilot can see!

00:04:56.614 --> 00:05:00.176
If the natural pull is permanently gone

00:05:00.237 --> 00:05:06.500
I'll engineer the weight just to carry on!

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.802
Making my own Artificial Gravity!

00:05:14.224 --> 00:05:17.200
I'll engineer the weight.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.105
The stalemate year.

00:05:21.446 --> 00:05:23.500
Artificial Gravity.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:06:00.000
[Outro — Acoustic Guitar Pattern Coming to a Controlled Stop]
